  "description": "DINTEC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C32 H74 Co5 Dy4 N4 O46,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.103-3.887 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.01-113.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C36H90N4O50Co5Dy4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
